# Verbatim material: not prose, and not fmt-md's business.
# Reformatting these is render-equivalent and still destructive — the line
# structure is part of what is being preserved — so no automatic check can
# catch it. Excluded by declaration. See arch/utils/fmt-md.

# Raw AI session transcripts (pasted shell, logs, tool output).
v2/.archived/second-pass/spikes/session-vault/raw/

# Provenanced copies of source material gathered for the needs work.
v2/udon-needs/01-ideation/02-provenanced/copies/

# Nested-fence examples (```udon containing an inner ``` fence): malformed
# CommonMark that every parser reads as the outer fence closing early, so
# fmt-md sees the code inside as joinable prose. Layout was hand-restored
# 2026-07-22 (commit 2ac2883); excluded so no future run re-flattens it.
# Real fix if ever wanted: 4-backtick outer fences (but these are archived
# archaeology — left verbatim).
v2/.archived/first-pass/greenfield-*/snippets/from-spec/CORE.md

# Carries a verbatim appendix: an agent's original first-encounter reading,
# reproduced unprocessed as the primary record, plus nested verbatim quotes
# inside each commentary callout. The whole point of both is that they are
# un-edited, so a render-equivalent reflow is exactly the silent damage this
# file exists to prevent. (Added 2026-07-30 after the file had already been
# fmt-md'd four times during authoring — no damage: the in-place runs all
# predate the appendix, and every --check since has reported clean.)
v2/theory/to-integrate/refine-more/de-novo-audit.md
